(1) Rust fp32: max|diff| vs torch 1.14e-05; acc 0.9741; weights 1204 kB
(2) Rust int8: max|diff| vs NumPy same-algorithm 0.00e+00; serial==parallel True; max|dlogit| vs fp32 0.162; acc 0.9741; argmax agree with fp32 1.0000; weights 308 kB
    Rust int8 vs ORT dynamic int8 logits: max|diff| 0.180 (different activation quantization scheme from ORT's DynamicQuantizeMatMul, so not bit-identical)
(3) median latency, us/call:
    torch eager fp32 (1 thread)    b1     30.1   b256     782.9
    ORT fp32 (1 thread)            b1     14.7   b256     683.8
    ORT dynamic int8 (1 thread)    b1     10.8   b256     212.8
    Rust fp32 serial               b1     17.0   b256    4279.5
    Rust int8 serial               b1     31.3   b256    8058.8
    Rust fp32 rayon (8 threads)    b1     16.9   b256     642.7
    Rust int8 rayon (8 threads)    b1     31.3   b256    1072.4
note: the Rust engine does one row at a time (matrix-vector); torch/ORT call a blocked GEMM for b256 (weights reused from cache across rows).
